{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up on your #11 commit. Same branch and fence rules as before. Do not delegate further. Make one new commit, do not amend, and do not push.\n\n1. src/doctor.rs: delete the `check_plugin_registration` option on `RunDoctorOpts`, the always-ok plugin-registration stub, and the `plugin_registration` field on the report. Remove every call site that passes `None`, including src/cli_info.rs and the MCP doctor path, and delete the tests that cover them.\n2. src/models.rs: replace `BackendNotImplementedError` with a plain boxed string error. The message must stay word for word the same. src/cli.rs already prints `{e}` for any error that is not a `ModelNotAllowedError`.\n3. src/cli_info.rs: derive the \"backend not implemented\" skip lines from the config, grouping models whose backend is not \"cursor\", instead of hardcoding `[\"pi\", \"claude\"]`.\n4. src/tool_schemas.rs: in the `requireNonClaude` description, change \"resolved model family is 'claude'\" to \"resolved model backend is 'claude'\".\n5. Deflake (issue #22). In tests/cli_e2e.rs, inside the `delegate()` helper, change `si.write_all(s.as_bytes()).unwrap();` to `let _ = si.write_all(s.as_bytes());`. The child can exit on bad input before it reads stdin, and the test asserts on the exit code. Make the same change in tests/cli_info_e2e.rs if it has the same pattern. Record the negative control: with the old `.unwrap()`, loop `cargo test --test cli_e2e bad_run_input_exits_2` 30 times and report how many runs fail. Then report the same with the fix in place.\n\nThen run `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test`. All must pass. End the commit message with `Co-Authored-By: Muse Spark 1.3 <noreply@opencode.ai>`.\n\nReport: the commit SHA, the test summary, and the negative-control counts. Then Friction, up to 3 bullets.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}],"timestamp":1790846638935}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up on your #11 commit. Same branch and fence rules as before. Do not delegate further. Make one new commit, do not amend, and do not push.\n\n1. src/doctor.rs: delete the `check_plugin_registration` option on `RunDoctorOpts`, the always-ok plugin-registration stub, and the `plugin_registration` field on the report. Remove every call site that passes `None`, including src/cli_info.rs and the MCP doctor path, and delete the tests that cover them.\n2. src/models.rs: replace `BackendNotImplementedError` with a plain boxed string error. The message must stay word for word the same. src/cli.rs already prints `{e}` for any error that is not a `ModelNotAllowedError`.\n3. src/cli_info.rs: derive the \"backend not implemented\" skip lines from the config, grouping models whose backend is not \"cursor\", instead of hardcoding `[\"pi\", \"claude\"]`.\n4. src/tool_schemas.rs: in the `requireNonClaude` description, change \"resolved model family is 'claude'\" to \"resolved model backend is 'claude'\".\n5. Deflake (issue #22). In tests/cli_e2e.rs, inside the `delegate()` helper, change `si.write_all(s.as_bytes()).unwrap();` to `let _ = si.write_all(s.as_bytes());`. The child can exit on bad input before it reads stdin, and the test asserts on the exit code. Make the same change in tests/cli_info_e2e.rs if it has the same pattern. Record the negative control: with the old `.unwrap()`, loop `cargo test --test cli_e2e bad_run_input_exits_2` 30 times and report how many runs fail. Then report the same with the fix in place.\n\nThen run `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test`. All must pass. End the commit message with `Co-Authored-By: Muse Spark 1.3 <noreply@opencode.ai>`.\n\nReport: the commit SHA, the test summary, and the negative-control counts. Then Friction, up to 3 bullets.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}],"timestamp":1790846638935}}
